            <ArticleTitle>The role of kinetocardiography in the complex study of the mechanical cardiac activity in ischemic heart disease.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>66-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The complex study of mechanical manifestations of cardiac activity by kinetocardiography, along with a complete clinical examination, is suggested as a rather sensitive method which precisely detects the changes of cardiodynamics in disturbances of the coronary circulation, rendering information useful in diagnosis and prognosis.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
